ase</article-title><source>Surg Today</source><year>2001</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>517</fpage><lpage>520</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11428605</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kurugoglu</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Aksoy</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kantarci</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Radiological work-up in Peutz-Jeghers syndrome</article-title><source>Pediatr Radiol</source><year>2003</year><volume>33</volume><fpage>766</fpage><lpage>771</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14508616</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>Manual resolution of bowel intussusception during the surgical procedure.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="crg0004-0452-f01"/></fig><fig id="F2" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><p>Intraluminal polyp after surgical resection.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="crg0004-0452-f02"/></fig><fig id="F3" orientation="portrait" position="float"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><p>Hyperplastic polyp epithelium is separated by branching bundles of smooth muscle.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="crg0004-0452-f03"/></fig></floats-group></article>